    "created_at": "2024-12-04T22:30:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-12-04T22:30:13Z",
    "body": "This behavior for chromium and webkit was implmented here:\r\n- https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/2477d2d429b537532afead1cb60e6a90f5581ff4%5E%21/\r\n- https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=36006\r\n\r\nBefore this patch, `<select multiple>` and `<select size=2>` were always rendered in-page for all platforms. I'm guessing that there was a desire to add native support for some platforms which had multi-select popups, and it was decided to do it this way, and the platforms which didn't have native support for multi-select popups continued to use the existing in-page listbox.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
