    "updated_at": "2025-08-07T15:27:22Z",
    "body": "The CSS Working Group just discussed `Rendering <select> as a listbox is a one-line widget that opens a popup on iOS and Android`.\n\n<details><summary>The full IRC log of that discussion</summary>\n&lt;zcorpan> jarhar: I want to have parity for mobile and desktop<br>\n&lt;zcorpan> jarhar: Ability to get either UX on both mobile and desktop<br>\n&lt;zcorpan> annevk: There's no native equivalent. Is a challenge<br>\n&lt;zcorpan> jarhar: I can't speak to the macOS native stuff... Current prototype in chrome uses popover to render the picker. Similar to appearance: base. But with more opinionated styles<br>\n&lt;zcorpan> jarhar: Maybe could implement as popover with !important styles?<br>\n&lt;zcorpan> jarhar: Can switch to native in the future if it becomes available<br>\n&lt;zcorpan> annevk: Possibly. Not sure if acceptable<br>\n&lt;zcorpan> jarhar: Would it be helpful if I create a demo?<br>\n&lt;zcorpan> annevk: Not needed, but thx<br>\n&lt;zcorpan> emilio: Agree with wanting to be able to make a listbox on mobile. No strong opinion on the design or specifics<br>\n</details>\n",
